div.p:
Story says CIA came to rely on NSA as means of developing potential recruits;
                    adds that officers of the four organizations played musical chairs in moving
                    from group to group.

note.p:
Source: Johnson Library, National Security File, Subject File, Box 44,
                        Ramparts—NSA—CIA. Confidential. Drafted by Geraldine Sheehan (G/Y), Robison, and Slocum;
                    cleared by Canter, German, and Walker; approved by Kohler. All brackets are in the original.
